WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:13.857
Pinocchio was lost.

2
00:00:13.858 --> 00:00:16.959
It seemed that no one had heard him cry for help.

3
00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:22.780
But just when he was about to lose hope, he heard footsteps.

4
00:00:22.781 --> 00:00:28.290
"Good afternoon, Pinocchio," said a fox as it walked up to him.

5
00:00:28.291 --> 00:00:30.600
The fox was leaning on a cane.

6
00:00:30.601 --> 00:00:34.991
To his side was a blind cat with bandages over his eyes.

7
00:00:34.992 --> 00:00:42.090
"Who are you?" asked Pinocchio. "How do you know my name?"

8
00:00:42.091 --> 00:00:46.604
"We have seen your father, Geppetto, calling for you in the village.

9
00:00:46.605 --> 00:00:53.879
He has asked all of the villagers for help, but no one knows where to find you," said the cat.

10
00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:57.883
"Poor father, searching for me in the cold.

11
00:00:57.884 --> 00:00:59.753
He must be worried.

12
00:00:59.754 --> 00:01:05.436
I must hurry home to show him we are rich," Pinocchio said.

13
00:01:05.437 --> 00:01:10.627
When they heard this, the cat peeked out from under the bandage and the fox stood straighter.

14
00:01:10.628 --> 00:01:12.723
But, Pinocchio did not notice.

15
00:01:12.724 --> 00:01:17.126
"What? Rich?" asked the fox.

16
00:01:17.127 --> 00:01:21.885
"How could a small wooden boy be rich?"

17
00:01:21.886 --> 00:01:27.075
"I . . . uh . . . I earned the money," Pinocchio lied.

18
00:01:27.076 --> 00:01:31.254
"Earned it? How?" asked the cat.

19
00:01:31.255 --> 00:01:38.822
"I worked as a dancer for the marionette master, and he paid me," Pinocchio lied again.

20
00:01:38.823 --> 00:01:44.785
"I don't believe such a small boy like you could have a lot of money.

21
00:01:44.786 --> 00:01:50.070
I would have to see it to believe such a thing," said the cat.

22
00:01:50.071 --> 00:01:54.260
"Well, you can't see it," said Pinocchio.

23
00:01:54.261 --> 00:01:56.372
"I have hidden it away."

24
00:01:56.373 --> 00:02:01.665
He didn't think about how strange it was for a blind cat to ask to see his gold.

25
00:02:01.666 --> 00:02:08.735
"It's a shame you can't take home more than a pocketful of money to Geppetto," said the fox.

26
00:02:08.736 --> 00:02:11.245
"He is such a kind man.

27
00:02:11.246 --> 00:02:20.651
I know of a way to make a small bit of money into a large load of money, but I'm sure you wouldn't be interested.

28
00:02:20.652 --> 00:02:26.577
Come, Mr. Cat, let's show Pinocchio the way home."

29
00:02:26.578 --> 00:02:29.434
"You mean I could have more money?"

30
00:02:29.435 --> 00:02:32.695
Pinocchio asked, surprised at this new idea.

31
00:02:32.696 --> 00:02:34.771
"Would I have to work for it?"

32
00:02:34.772 --> 00:02:39.073
"Oh no!" the cat said, laughing.

33
00:02:39.074 --> 00:02:43.109
"We would never suggest such a silly thing.

34
00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:47.231
We know of a secret field called the Field of Follies.

35
00:02:47.232 --> 00:02:58.196
If you plant your money in that field at midnight, water it, and come back the next day, it will have grown into a money tree."

36
00:02:58.197 --> 00:03:02.985
"Wow, then we would be really rich!" Pinocchio said.

37
00:03:02.986 --> 00:03:07.791
He could imagine Mr. Cricket telling him that honest work was the best way to be rich.

38
00:03:07.792 --> 00:03:13.288
"But, Geppetto would love me so much more if I was rich now.

39
00:03:13.289 --> 00:03:18.903
Please, would you show me this Field of Follies?"

40
00:03:18.904 --> 00:03:21.859
So, off they went to find the Field of Follies.

41
00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:27.609
They walked all day and into the evening.

42
00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:32.386
"Welcome to the Field of Follies, Pinocchio," said the cat.

43
00:03:32.387 --> 00:03:37.844
"Plant your gold wherever you want your money tree to grow!"

44
00:03:37.845 --> 00:03:39.812
Pinocchio was very excited.

45
00:03:39.813 --> 00:03:45.767
He dug a hole, carefully placed his gold inside, and covered the hole with dirt.

46
00:03:45.768 --> 00:03:48.224
"Now, you must water it.

47
00:03:48.225 --> 00:03:55.017
Mr. Cat and I will guard the money while you run to get some water," said the fox.

48
00:03:55.018 --> 00:03:59.509
Pinocchio did not think it was strange for a blind cat to stand guard.

49
00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:03.244
He ran off and quickly returned with a bucket of water.

50
00:04:03.245 --> 00:04:08.649
After the gold had been watered, there was nothing left to do but wait.

51
00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:14.626
"Now, let's go find a nearby barn so we can rest," said the cat.

52
00:04:14.627 --> 00:04:22.081
"Yes, if we stay here and watch, the tree will not grow," agreed the fox.

53
00:04:22.082 --> 00:04:28.410
So, off they went with happy thoughts of being rich.
